From 0021eb2ee975c0940dc827568c73fa3890b4187c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:52:44 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 58/61] Input: tell a port whether player 1 has a gamepad, and
 unplug the script's first pad

Extension interface 7 adds first_pad_connected(): player 1 has a gamepad,
not only the keyboard. A port with local multiplayer uses it to notice
player 1's gamepad going away mid-game, as second_pad().connected does for
player 2's.

The input script gains `detach` and `attach` for its first virtual pad, as
`detach2` and `attach2` do for the second, so that losing player 1's pad can
be tested.

Tested with Dissidia 012 (local versus, Windows): both pads unplugged and
plugged in again in a scripted battle.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
